WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.940
Tesla built its first cybercab using cathode material made at the new gigatexas plant. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 615. The first cybercab used cathode active material made inside the new plant at gigatexas. That plant receives lithium hydroxide from the nearby Robstown refinery. The arrangement replaces an 8,000 mile overseas route with a loop under 200 miles inside Texas. Engineers can now set the exact particle shape in coding

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.680
chemistry required for the dry electrode process.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.740
Each ton of cathode material therefore supports nearly three times as many cybercabs as it

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:39.860
would for a heavier truck.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.560
Tesla also qualifies for layered manufacturing credits under the Inflation Reduction Act

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.820
at every stage from cathode to pack.

